{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795626233,"nonce":"bkmX5w0Ut8r8QGJ8t4JpPNcWxcU=","title":"The cn code editor's find bar covers the first lines and the matches under it","message":"The bar floats over the top right of the editor. Matches on the lines behind it are hidden, and stepping to one does not move it clear of the bar. In a narrow or short editor the bar covers most of the visible code.\n\nWanted, either or both:\n- while the bar is open, room above the first line equal to the bar's height, so the top of the file can scroll below it;\n- stepping to a match scrolls it below the bar.\n\nBoth need the layout editor to take a top inset that rows, gutter, caret, selection, hit testing and scroll-into-view all honour, set from outside as `find_open` is.","files":null}]}